      "finding": "The current emitted availability requires governing party slot 4 throughout; Aziz also requires the actual office-holder. Thus a government studies a Road to Power, organizes a Democratic Opposition and establishes underground cells; the important historical Baath-front/legalization struggle cannot be played while the Baath governs. Localization confirms this is not merely an abstract intelligence programme.",
      "proposal": "Separate pre-accession opposition/coalition activity from the government programme. Keep consent-based legalization and front negotiations in political decisions under the incumbent; bring their result into the later ICP government. Recast governing cards as coalition cabinet rights, internal party organization and returning exiled cadres, or explicitly unlock a bounded opposition chapter without granting government-bound buffs. Do not activate the entire Communist state programme from a coalition seat alone. No proposed geometry until that political contract is selected.",
