      "finding": "Seek Gulf Backing is a short-war-only optional dead end; Secure Foreign Spares is a sustained-war-only optional dead end. Credit and foreign spare parts were not mutually incompatible needs tied to those respective operational plans. Each adds 21 focus days merely to unlock a recipient negotiation. This concerns the direct unlock inside the Iran chapter, not every possible credit source: COLDWAR_IRQ_saddam_credit also unlocks decision_gulf_credit, whose creditor options call COLDWAR_IRQ_gulf_unlock_credit (decisions_module.py302-305), so a sustained-war player can obtain credit through that separate route.",
      "proposal": "Preferred smaller structure: merge both decision unlocks into iran_operational_plan, preserving all actual consent, treasury, debt, equipment and supplier checks. Retire the two standalone unlock-only cards from the proposed next revision, never delete their decisions or ledgers. If dedicated focuses are desired, both must be shared optional support spurs accessible from either plan, not new mutual exclusions.",
